 ('Mishnah Tahorot 5:2', 'CONTEXT', "'I touched one but do not know which' — the same doubt rule; R. Yose's path exception."),
 ('Mishnah Tahorot 5:3', 'OUTSIDE', "the two paths and the two foods in sequence — not this span's."),
 ('Mishnah Tahorot 5:4', 'OUTSIDE', "the sheretz and the frog in sequence — not this span's."),
 ('Mishnah Tahorot 5:5', 'OUTSIDE', "two men on two paths asking together or apart — not this span's."),
 ('Mishnah Tahorot 5:6', 'OUTSIDE', "the two loaves — not this span's."),
 ('Mishnah Tahorot 5:7', 'OUTSIDE', "the public domain's clothes and spit; the sleeper; the corpse found in the morning — not this span's."),
 ('Mishnah Tahorot 5:8', 'OUTSIDE', "the town's spit; the woman in the boat — not this span's."),
 ('Mishnah Tahorot 5:9', 'OUTSIDE', "the witnesses to impurity — not this span's (the sotah's witness rule is its own, Sotah 2a)."),
 ('Mishnah Tahorot 6:1', 'OUTSIDE', "a place changing domain — not this span's."),
 ('Mishnah Tahorot 6:2', 'OUTSIDE', "R. Yehoshua's four doubts — not this span's."),
 ('Mishnah Tahorot 6:3', 'OUTSIDE', "the tree, the hole, the shop — not this span's."),
 ('Mishnah Tahorot 6:4', 'CONTEXT', "'however many doubts you multiply, a doubt in a PRIVATE DOMAIN is unclean' — the rule derived from the sotah (secluded, private, doubtful — unclean: Sotah 28a); the mishnah's own domain purity."),
 ('Mishnah Tahorot 6:5', 'OUTSIDE', "the valley in the rainy season — not this span's."),
 ('Mishnah Tahorot 6:6', 'OUTSIDE', "what counts as a public domain — not this span's."),
 ('Mishnah Tahorot 6:7', 'OUTSIDE', "the valley by season — not this span's."),
 ('Mishnah Tahorot 6:8', 'OUTSIDE', "the basilica — not this span's."),
 ('Mishnah Tahorot 6:9', 'OUTSIDE', "the covered forum — not this span's."),
 ('Mishnah Tahorot 6:10', 'OUTSIDE', "the colonnades and the courtyard — not this span's."),
 ('Mishnah Sotah 1:1', 'LAW', "THE ANSWER SHEET: the warning before two witnesses (R. Eliezer; R. Yehoshua); the drinking on one witness or himself (R. Eliezer) / two (R. Yehoshua). CELL sotah('witnesses', warning|seclusion); the row sotah_witness_counts."),
 ('Mishnah Sotah 1:2', 'LAW', "THE ANSWER SHEET: 'do not speak with so-and-so' and she spoke — permitted; secluded long enough to be defiled — FORBIDDEN TO HER HOME, barred from terumah (a priest's wife), and if he died childless she performs chalitzah, not levirate marriage. CELL sotah('doubt_forbids'), ('levirate')."),
 ('Mishnah Sotah 1:3', 'LAW', "THE ANSWER SHEET: barred from terumah — 'I am defiled'; witnesses; 'I will not drink'; the husband unwilling; he cohabited on the way. THE PROCEDURE: he brings her to the local court; TWO SCHOLARS accompany (R. Yehuda: trusted). CELL sotah('who_does_not_drink'), ('escort')."),
 ('Mishnah Sotah 1:4', 'LAW', "THE ANSWER SHEET: brought to the Sanhedrin in Jerusalem; threatened as capital witnesses are; 'wine, levity, immaturity, bad neighbors'; 'act for the great Name, that it not be erased on the water'. CELL sotah('court'), ('admonition')."),
 ('Mishnah Sotah 1:5', 'LAW', "THE ANSWER SHEET: 'I am defiled' — she writes a receipt for her marriage contract and is divorced; 'I am pure' — the Eastern Gate (Nicanor), where sotahs drink, women after birth and lepers are purified; the priest tears her clothes to her heart and unbraids her hair (R. Yehuda: unless attractive). CELL sotah('confesses') -> receipt, divorced; ('place'); ('uncovering')."),
 ('Mishnah Sotah 1:6', 'LAW', "THE ANSWER SHEET: black garments; her adornments removed; the Egyptian rope above her breasts; anyone may watch except her slaves; all women should watch (Ezek 23:48). CELL sotah('uncovering', details)."),
 ('Mishnah Sotah 1:7', 'LAW', "THE ANSWER SHEET: MEASURE FOR MEASURE — she adorned herself, is made unattractive; exposed herself, is exposed; began with the thigh then the belly, so the thigh first (Sotah 9b). THE MIDDOT'S CASE LAW: the mishnah the Beha'alotcha reading cited (Sifrei 106:1 = Mishnah Sotah 1:9). CELL sotah('outcome', guilty) -> the thigh first, the belly, the whole body."),
 ('Mishnah Sotah 1:8', 'CONTEXT', "Samson's eyes, Absalom's hair, the ten spears, the three thefts — measure for measure in the stories; not this span's cell."),
 ('Mishnah Sotah 1:9', 'CONTEXT', "Miriam's hour for Moses and Israel's SEVEN DAYS for her (12:15 — Beha'alotcha's seat); Joseph's and Moses' burials — the reward's measure."),
 ('Mishnah Sotah 2:1', 'LAW', "THE ANSWER SHEET: the minchah in an Egyptian basket placed in her hands to fatigue her; its beginning in the basket, its end in a service vessel; NO OIL, NO FRANKINCENSE; of BARLEY, unsifted (Rabban Gamliel: an animal's food for an animal's deed). CELL sotah('minchah_form')."),
 ('Mishnah Sotah 2:6', 'LAW', "THE ANSWER SHEET: the oath cannot cover before betrothal or after divorce; nor a divorced period's defilement (which would not forbid her): only what would forbid her to him. CELL sotah('oath_scope') -> only forbidding acts."),
 ('Mishnah Sotah 3:1', 'LAW', "THE ANSWER SHEET: the minchah from the basket into a service vessel, on her hand; the priest's hand under hers, WAVED TOGETHER. CELL sotah('waving') -> together."),
 ('Mishnah Sotah 3:3', 'LAW', "THE ANSWER SHEET: 'I will not drink' before the erasure — the scroll sequestered, the minchah burned in the ash-place, the scroll unfit for another; 'I am defiled' after the erasure — the water poured out; 'I will not drink' after the erasure — FORCED. CELL sotah('refuses', when)."),
 ('Mishnah Sotah 3:4', 'LAW', "THE ANSWER SHEET: the guilty one's face greens, eyes bulge, veins protrude before she finishes — 'remove her'; MERIT delays one, two, three years (Ben Azzai: teach your daughter Torah; R. Eliezer: promiscuity; R. Yehoshua's kav). CELL sotah('outcome', guilty|merit); the row merit_suspends' year settings."),
 ('Mishnah Sotah 3:5', 'DISPUTE', "R. Shimon: merit does NOT delay (else the waters weakened and the innocent defamed); Rebbi: delays but she wastes away and dies the same death. The row merit_suspends' 'none' setting and Rebbi's rider."),
 ('Mishnah Sotah 3:6', 'LAW', "THE ANSWER SHEET: her minchah impure before the service vessel — redeemed; after — burned; BURNED for: 'I am defiled', witnesses, 'I will not drink', the husband unwilling, he cohabited on the way; every priest's wife's minchah burned (Lev 6:16). CELL sotah('minchah_disposition', case)."),
 ('Mishnah Sotah 3:7', 'LAW', "THE ANSWER SHEET: an Israelite woman married to a priest — burned; a priest's daughter married to an Israelite — eaten; the priest against the priest's daughter (disqualified, impure for the dead, the most holy). CELL sotah('minchah_disposition', priests_wife|priests_daughter)."),
 ('Mishnah Sotah 3:8', 'LAW', "THE ANSWER SHEET: man and woman — the leper's hair and garments; A MAN VOWS HIS MINOR SON A NAZIRITE, a woman not; a man shaves on his father's naziriteship funds, a woman not; betrothal, sale, stoning naked, hanging, sold for theft. CELL nazirite('father_vows_son'), ('shaves_on_fathers_funds') (Mishnah Nazir 4:6-7)."),
 ('Mishnah Sotah 4:2', 'LAW', "THE ANSWER SHEET: neither drink nor collect — 'I am defiled', witnesses, 'I will not drink'; the husband's refusal or his cohabitation on the way — collect but do not drink; the husband died — Shammai: collect, no drink / Hillel: drink or no ketubah. CELL sotah('who_does_not_drink', ketubah); the row husband_died_ketubah."),
 ('Mishnah Sotah 4:3', 'LAW', "THE ANSWER SHEET: pregnant or nursing another's child at marriage — neither (R. Meir) / the Rabbis: drink; the AILONIT, the elderly, the infertile — neither (R. Elazar: drink); all others drink or forfeit. CELL sotah('status', pregnant|nursing|ailonit); the rows ailonit_drinks, pregnant_drinks."),
 ('Mishnah Sotah 4:4', 'LAW', "THE ANSWER SHEET: the priest's wife drinks and is permitted; the eunuch's wife drinks; warning about all forbidden relatives, not a minor nor a non-man. CELL sotah('status'), ('warned_about')."),
 ('Mishnah Sotah 4:5', 'LAW', "THE ANSWER SHEET: the court warns the wife of a deaf-mute, an imbecile, a prisoner — to disqualify her ketubah (the Sages) / R. Yosei: to drink when he returns. CELL sotah('court_warns'); the row court_warning_effect."),
 ('Mishnah Sotah 5:2', 'OUTSIDE', "R. Akiva on Lev 11:33's 'shall be impure' (third-degree impurity) — 'on that day'; not this span's."),
 ('Mishnah Sotah 5:3', 'CONTEXT', "R. Akiva on Num 35:4-5: one thousand cubits the open land, TWO THOUSAND THE SABBATH LIMIT (R. Eliezer b. R. Yosei HaGelili: fields and vineyards) — BAMIDBAR'S FORWARD POINTER CONFIRMED on the answer sheet: the two thousand cubits live at Num 35:5 (Masei's walk), not at 2:2."),
 ('Mishnah Sotah 5:4', 'OUTSIDE', "R. Akiva on 'saying' at the Song (Exod 15:1) — the responsive song; the exodus story's."),
 ('Mishnah Sotah 5:5', 'OUTSIDE', "R. Yehoshua ben Hyrcanus on Job's love — not this span's."),
 ('Mishnah Sotah 6:1', 'LAW', "THE ANSWER SHEET: warned and secluded, heard 'from a flying bird' — R. Eliezer: divorces her but pays the ketubah; R. Yehoshua: not until the spinners by moonlight discuss her. CELL sotah('rumor') (the row sotah_witness_counts' consequence)."),
 ('Mishnah Sotah 6:2', 'LAW', "THE ANSWER SHEET: one witness 'she was defiled' — she does not drink (divorced); a slave or maidservant believed to bar the ketubah; her mother-in-law and the four other women believed only to bar the drinking, not the ketubah. CELL sotah('witness_of_defilement', who) -> the credibility ladder."),
 ('Mishnah Sotah 6:4', 'LAW', "THE ANSWER SHEET: one says defiled and one not (or two women) — she DRINKS; one against two — drinks; two against one — does not drink, divorced. CELL sotah('contradicting_witnesses')."),
 ('Mishnah Sotah 7:1', 'LAW', "THE ANSWER SHEET: recited in any language — the sotah's portion, the tithe declaration, Shema, the Amidah, Grace, the oaths of testimony and deposit. CELL sotah('language') -> any."),
 ('Mishnah Sotah 7:6', 'LAW', "THE ANSWER SHEET: the blessing — in the province three blessings with amen, in the Temple one with 'Blessed be the LORD... from eternity to eternity'; the Name as written in the Temple, the substitute outside; the hands at the shoulders / above the head, the High Priest not above the frontplate (R. Yehuda: even he). CELL blessing('form', place)."),
 ('Mishnah Sotah 9:9', 'LAW', "THE ANSWER SHEET: when adulterers multiplied THE BITTER WATERS WERE ABOLISHED — Rabban Yochanan ben Zakkai, by Hosea 4:14 (with the heifer's abolition and the clusters' end). THE DATA ROW waters_abolished: abolished (the tradition's setting) / running (the ink's, the tape's)."),
 ('Mishnah Nazir 1:2', 'LAW', "THE ANSWER SHEET: 'a nazirite from seeds / skins / shaving / impurity' — a full nazirite; 'like Samson, the son of Manoah, Delilah's husband, the gates of Gaza, the gouged eyes' — a Samson-nazirite; the permanent nazirite lightens with a razor and brings three, the Samson-nazirite never shaves and brings none for impurity. CELL nazirite('vow_form', partial|samson|permanent)."),
 ('Mishnah Nazir 1:3', 'LAW', "THE ANSWER SHEET: unspecified — THIRTY DAYS; 'one long term', 'one short term', 'till the end of the world' — thirty; 'and one day', 'and one hour', 'one and a half' — TWO terms; 'thirty days and an hour' — thirty-one (no hours). CELL nazirite('term', form) -> 30 / 60 / 31 (the data row nazir_default_days)."),
 ('Mishnah Nazir 1:4', 'LAW', "THE ANSWER SHEET: 'like the hairs of my head, the dust, the sand' — a nazirite FOREVER, shaving every thirty days; Rebbi: one long term, no shaving; the plural 'naziriteships' shaves every thirty. CELL nazirite('term', like_the_hairs); PARAMETER ROW hairs_vow_shaving: the first tanna / Rebbi."),
 ('Mishnah Nazir 1:5', 'LAW', "THE ANSWER SHEET: 'as the house's capacity, the basket's' — asked his intent: one long term — thirty; unspecified — as mustard seeds fill the basket, a nazirite for life. CELL nazirite('term', capacity)."),
 ('Mishnah Nazir 1:6', 'LAW', "THE ANSWER SHEET: 'from here to such a place' — the days of the walk; under thirty — thirty. CELL nazirite('term', distance) -> max(30, days of the journey)."),
 ('Mishnah Nazir 1:7', 'LAW', "THE ANSWER SHEET: 'as the days of the solar year' — 365 consecutive terms (R. Yehuda's incident: he died at their end). CELL nazirite('term', solar_year) -> 365 terms."),
 ('Mishnah Nazir 2:1', 'DISPUTE', "'a nazirite from dried figs' — Beit Shammai: a nazirite; Beit Hillel: not; R. Yehuda: Shammai meant a konam on figs. The row erroneous_nazir_vow (Nazir 9a)."),
 ('Mishnah Nazir 2:2', 'DISPUTE', "'this cow said: I am a nazirite if I stand up', 'this door...' — Shammai / Hillel; R. Yehuda's konam reading. The same row."),
 ('Mishnah Nazir 2:3', 'LAW', "THE ANSWER SHEET: a cup poured and 'I am a nazirite from it' — a full nazirite; the intoxicated woman's cup — a konam on that cup only (the Sages). CELL nazirite('vow_form', from_the_cup) -> nazirite; the drunk woman's exception."),
 ('Mishnah Nazir 2:4', 'LAW', "THE ANSWER SHEET: 'a nazirite on condition that I may drink wine and become impure' — a full nazirite; 'I did not know a nazirite is forbidden wine' — bound (R. Shimon: free); 'I thought the Sages would permit me because I cannot live without wine / I bury the dead' — free (R. Shimon: bound). CELL nazirite('vow_form', conditioned|mistaken); PARAMETER ROW nazir_vow_scope."),
 ('Mishnah Nazir 2:5', 'LAW', "THE ANSWER SHEET: 'I am a nazirite and will shave a nazirite' and another 'I too' — both nazirites who pay for a nazirite's offerings; if wise, they shave each other. CELL nazirite('shave_a_nazirite') -> each other."),
 ('Mishnah Nazir 2:6', 'DISPUTE', "'to shave HALF a nazirite' twice — R. Meir: each a whole (no half nazirite); the Rabbis: each half. PARAMETER ROW half_nazirite: the Rabbis / R. Meir."),
 ('Mishnah Nazir 2:7', 'LAW', "THE ANSWER SHEET: 'a nazirite when I have a SON' — a daughter, a tumtum, a hermaphrodite: not; 'a CHILD' — any. CELL nazirite('conditioned_on_birth', son|child, born)."),
 ('Mishnah Nazir 2:8', 'LAW', "THE ANSWER SHEET: a miscarriage — not a nazirite (R. Shimon: the viability condition and a voluntary naziriteship); born again — a nazirite (R. Shimon's second condition). CELL nazirite('conditioned_on_birth', miscarriage); R. Shimon's arm recorded."),
 ('Mishnah Nazir 2:9', 'LAW', "THE ANSWER SHEET: 'a nazirite now, and when I have a son' — his own term first, then the son's; reversed — the son's interrupts and his own completes after. CELL nazirite('two_terms_order')."),
 ('Mishnah Nazir 2:10', 'LAW', "THE ANSWER SHEET: 'when I have a son' + 'a hundred days from now' — born within SEVENTY days: nothing lost (thirty for the son, then the remainder); after seventy — the seventy negated (no shaving under thirty days apart). CELL nazirite('two_terms_order', hundred_days, born_on_day) -> the seventy rule."),
 ('Mishnah Nazir 3:1', 'LAW', "THE ANSWER SHEET: unspecified — shaves on the THIRTY-FIRST; on the thirtieth fulfilled; 'for thirty days' — the thirtieth not fulfilled. CELL nazirite('shaving_day', term_form) -> 31 / 30 counts / 30 stated needs 31 (THE TIMER's due on the scene)."),
 ('Mishnah Nazir 3:2', 'LAW', "THE ANSWER SHEET: two terms — the first on the 31st, the second on the 61st; shaved the first on the 30th — the second on the 60th; on the 59th fulfilled (R. Pappeyas' testimony: the thirtieth counts for both). CELL nazirite('shaving_day', two_terms) -> 31/61, 30/60, 59."),
 ('Mishnah Nazir 3:3', 'LAW', "THE ANSWER SHEET: unspecified, impure on the THIRTIETH — negates ALL (R. Eliezer: seven); 'for thirty days', impure on the thirtieth — all agree: all. CELL nazirite('what_negates', impurity, on_day) -> all; the row impure_on_last_day."),
 ('Mishnah Nazir 3:4', 'LAW', "THE ANSWER SHEET: 'a hundred days' — impure on the HUNDREDTH: all (R. Eliezer: thirty); on the 101st before the offerings: thirty (R. Eliezer: seven). CELL nazirite('what_negates', impurity, hundred_days, day) -> all / thirty; R. Eliezer's arm (the Sifrei 31:1's 'ninety-ninth voids all, hundredth thirty' beside it — the shelf's two numbers recorded)."),
 ('Mishnah Nazir 3:6', 'LAW', "THE ANSWER SHEET: vowed a long term ABROAD and came to the land — Shammai: thirty more; Hillel: ALL again (Queen Helene's twenty-one years; R. Yehuda: fourteen). CELL nazirite('vowed_abroad') -> Hillel's all; PARAMETER ROW abroad_recount: Hillel / Shammai."),
 ('Mishnah Nazir 3:7', 'DISPUTE', "two pairs of witnesses — two terms / five terms: Shammai — the testimony divided, no naziriteship; Hillel — two are within five: two. PARAMETER ROW divided_testimony: Hillel (running) / Shammai."),
 ('Mishnah Nazir 4:1', 'LAW', "THE ANSWER SHEET: 'I am a nazirite' — 'and I' — 'and I': all nazirites; the first dissolved — all dissolved; the last — he alone; 'my mouth like his mouth, my hair like his hair' — a nazirite; the wife's 'and I' — he may nullify hers, his stands; his 'and I' after hers — he cannot (his own would fall). CELL nazirite('chained_vows', which_dissolved), ('spouse_and_i')."),
 ('Mishnah Nazir 4:2', 'LAW', "THE ANSWER SHEET: 'I am a nazirite, and you' — 'amen': he may nullify hers, his stands; she 'and you' — 'amen': he cannot nullify. CELL nazirite('spouse_and_i', who_first)."),
 ('Mishnah Nazir 4:3', 'LAW', "THE ANSWER SHEET: a nazirite woman who drank and defiled herself — FORTY lashes each; her husband nullified without her knowing — no lashes (R. Yehuda: lashes of rebellion). CELL nazirite('lashes', woman, nullified_unknown) -> none (R. Yehuda's makkat mardut recorded)."),
 ('Mishnah Nazir 4:4', 'LAW', "THE ANSWER SHEET: her animals after nullification — his: graze; hers: the sin-offering DIES, the burnt-offering offered, the peace-offering eaten a day without loaves; unallocated funds — communal gifts; allocated — the sin-offering's to the Dead Sea, the burnt's an olah (misuse), the peace's a shelamim a day without loaves. CELL nazirite('nullified_after_separation', whose, allocated)."),
 ('Mishnah Nazir 4:6', 'LAW', "THE ANSWER SHEET: a man vows his MINOR SON a nazirite (a woman not); the son shaves, or is shaved, or objects, or his relatives object — cancelled; the animals as 4:4. CELL nazirite('father_vows_son', objection) -> cancelled."),
 ('Mishnah Nazir 4:7', 'LAW', "THE ANSWER SHEET: a man shaves on his FATHER'S naziriteship funds (a woman not) — only a son who was a nazirite in his father's lifetime with unallocated money left (R. Yosei: after the death — gifts). CELL nazirite('shaves_on_fathers_funds', when_vowed)."),
 ('Mishnah Nazir 5:1', 'DISPUTE', "erroneous consecration — Shammai: consecrated; Hillel: not ('the black bull first' and a white emerged). PARAMETER ROW erroneous_consecration: Hillel (running) / Shammai (the nazirite's erroneous vows the chapter's frame)."),
 ('Mishnah Nazir 5:2', 'DISPUTE', "the gold dinar, the barrel of wine — the same dispute. The same row."),
 ('Mishnah Nazir 5:3', 'LAW', "THE ANSWER SHEET: regretted, drank, asked and was NOT released — counts from the vow (the days he broke it count); RELEASED — the animal grazes (an erroneous consecration, Hillel to Shammai; the tithe's ninth and eleventh a Torah edict). CELL nazirite('dissolved_by_sage', released) -> the animal grazes / the count from the vow."),
 ('Mishnah Nazir 5:4', 'LAW', "THE ANSWER SHEET: vowed then the animal stolen — a nazirite; the animal stolen THEN vowed — not (an error from the outset); NACHUM THE MEDE'S ERROR at the Temple's destruction (before the destruction — nazirites; after — not). CELL nazirite('vow_in_error', event_before_or_after)."),
 ('Mishnah Nazir 5:5', 'DISPUTE', "the six walkers' conditional vows on the approaching man — Shammai: all nazirites; Hillel: only whose statement failed; R. Tarfon: none (explicitness). PARAMETER ROW uncertain_vow (Nazir 34a)."),
 ('Mishnah Nazir 5:6', 'LAW', "THE ANSWER SHEET: the man turned back — NONE is a nazirite (a doubtful naziriteship is lenient — Tahorot 4:7, 4:12); R. Shimon: each says 'if as I said, obligatory; if not, voluntary'. CELL nazirite('doubtful_vow') -> lenient; R. Shimon's arm."),
 ('Mishnah Nazir 5:7', 'LAW', "THE ANSWER SHEET: the KOY (wild / domestic / both / neither) and the nine conditional vows — ALL nazirites. CELL nazirite('doubtful_vow', koy) -> all bound (the koy's doubt an entity-doubt, not an event-doubt)."),
 ('Mishnah Nazir 6:1', 'LAW', "THE ANSWER SHEET: THREE prohibitions — impurity, shaving, the vine; the vine's products combine; an olive's bulk; a quarter-log of wine (the first mishnah) / R. Akiva: an olive's bulk with soaked bread. CELL nazirite('prohibitions'), ('ate')."),
 ('Mishnah Nazir 6:3', 'LAW', "THE ANSWER SHEET: unspecified thirty; shaved or SHAVED BY BANDITS — negates THIRTY; scissors, razor, plucked any amount — liable; may shampoo and separate by hand, not COMB (R. Yishmael: not with earth). CELL nazirite('what_negates', shaving) -> thirty; ('shaving_means'); ('grooming')."),
 ('Mishnah Nazir 6:4', 'LAW', "THE ANSWER SHEET: drinking all day one set; per warning each — likewise shaving and impurity. CELL nazirite('lashes_count')."),
 ('Mishnah Nazir 6:5', 'LAW', "THE ANSWER SHEET: impurity and shaving negate (all / thirty), the vine does not; the vine has NO exemptions, impurity and shaving have (the leper's obligatory shaving, the met mitzvah); impurity negates all with an offering, shaving thirty without. CELL nazirite('what_negates'); ('exemptions')."),
 ('Mishnah Nazir 6:6', 'LAW', "THE ANSWER SHEET: THE IMPURITY SHAVING — sprinkled on the third and seventh, shaves on the SEVENTH, brings on the EIGHTH; shaved on the eighth — brings that day (R. Akiva; R. Tarfon's leper objection: the nazirite's purity hangs on his days, the leper's on his shaving and the sunset). CELL nazirite('defiled', day_schedule) -> 3 / 7 / 8 (THE TIMER's re-set on the scene)."),
 ('Mishnah Nazir 6:7', 'LAW', "THE ANSWER SHEET: THE PURITY SHAVING — three animals (sin, burnt, peace); shaves after the PEACE-offering's slaughter (R. Yehuda) / after the SIN-offering's (R. Elazar); after any one — fulfilled. CELL nazirite('completion', shaves_after); PARAMETER ROW shaves_after: R. Yehuda / R. Elazar."),
 ('Mishnah Nazir 6:8', 'LAW', "THE ANSWER SHEET: three unspecified animals sorted by fitness (a ewe-lamb the sin, a lamb the burnt, a ram the peace); the hair under the peace-offering's pot; shaved in the province — not thrown; the impurity shaving — not thrown (R. Meir: all except the impure in the province). CELL nazirite('completion', sort_animals), ('hair_under_pot', where|which_shaving)."),
 ('Mishnah Nazir 6:10', 'LAW', "THE ANSWER SHEET: shaved on an offering found INVALID — the shaving invalid, the offerings not counted; on the sin-offering not for its name; on the burnt or peace not for its name (R. Shimon: that one alone fails); on all three with one valid — the shaving valid, the rest owed. CELL nazirite('shaved_on_invalid', which); the row shaved_on_invalid."),
 ('Mishnah Nazir 6:11', 'LAW', "THE ANSWER SHEET: the blood of ONE offering sprinkled, then impure — R. Eliezer: negates all; the Rabbis: brings the rest and is pure (MIRIAM OF TARMOD). CELL nazirite('impure_after_first_blood') -> the Rabbis; PARAMETER ROW impure_after_first_blood: the Rabbis / R. Eliezer."),
 ('Mishnah Nazir 7:1', 'LAW', "THE ANSWER SHEET: the High Priest and the nazirite become impure for a MET MITZVAH, not for relatives; both on the road and one corpse — R. Eliezer: the priest (no offering); the Rabbis: the nazirite (his holiness not permanent). CELL nazirite('met_mitzvah_with_high_priest'); PARAMETER ROW who_defiles_for_met_mitzvah: the Rabbis / R. Eliezer."),
